Grove PATCH-30: pwndaRecoverStalledBid must recover a bid parked in BID_ERROR
ON the timelock path, not decline it

PATCH-11's Gate 2 reads, in full:

    # Gate 2 -- a refund in flight means the timelock path owns the
    # funds now. Re-queueing a redeem against it is the one genuinely
    # unsafe thing this could do.
    if TxTypes.XMR_SWAP_A_LOCK_REFUND in bid.txns:
        return {
            "recovered": False,
            "state": state_before,
            "reason": "A refund is already in flight for this swap; the timelock path will complete it.",
        }

The first half is right and stays: re-queueing a chain-A REDEEM against a bid
whose lock has already moved into the refund tx is the unsafe thing, and it
must not happen. The second half is the bug. "The timelock path will complete
it" is stated as a fact about a bid that Gate 1 has just established is in
BID_ERROR -- and BID_ERROR is precisely the state in which the timelock path is
NOT running. checkXmrBidState has no BID_ERROR branch, so the bid is never
re-examined and nothing publishes the refund spend or the swipe.

So the gate declines to act on the grounds that something else will handle it,
where that something else is the exact thing that has stopped. This is the
"precondition copied from a neighbouring operation" shape: it is a correct
precondition for the REDEEM this function used to be the only way to trigger,
and it was carried onto the function as a whole.

The cost is not hypothetical. Live mainnet bid 000000006a9c9d96...9bb980,
2026-09-07: taker on LTC/XMR, both legs locked, counterparty gone, lock-refund
tx confirmed on chain, waiting for the coin-A swipe that would pay this side
the LTC it was buying. A transient Monero daemon outage tripped the (defective,
see PATCH-29) RPC-error escalation and parked it in BID_ERROR. The supervisor's
janitor (swap_bid.rs) POSTed pwndarecover on schedule, as designed -- and got
`recovered: false` with the sentence above, every time, for seven hours. The
swap survived only because the node happened to be restarted, which re-derives
state from chain outside this code path entirely.

The fix: when a refund IS in flight, put the bid back ON the timelock path
instead of declining. The state restored is XMR_SWAP_SCRIPT_TX_PREREFUND, which
is not a chosen state -- it is the one process_XMR_SWAP_A_LOCK_tx_spend sets on
seeing exactly the fact this branch has just tested for (the coin-A lock spent
into the lock-refund tx). The chain already justifies it; this only stops the
engine having forgotten. No transaction is built, nothing is published, and the
engine's own maturity checks decide what happens next, as they would have if
the bid had never been parked.

Still refused, unchanged: any bid not in BID_ERROR (Gate 1), and the chain-A
REDEEM re-queue against a refunding bid -- that path is now unreachable for
such a bid, which is what Gate 2 was protecting in the first place.

Idempotent: calling it on a bid already at PREREFUND is a no-op reassertion of
the state it is in.

Not an upstream candidate: pwndaRecoverStalledBid is ours (PATCH-11).

--- a/basicswap/basicswap.py
+++ b/basicswap/basicswap.py
@@ -7716,10 +7716,31 @@
             # funds now. Re-queueing a redeem against it is the one genuinely
             # unsafe thing this could do.
             if TxTypes.XMR_SWAP_A_LOCK_REFUND in bid.txns:
+                # PWNDA-PATCH-30: ...and that redeem is exactly what is NOT
+                # done here. But this used to RETURN, on the reasoning that
+                # "the timelock path will complete it" -- false for the only
+                # bids that reach this function. Gate 1 has just established
+                # BID_ERROR, and BID_ERROR is the state in which the timelock
+                # path is NOT running: checkXmrBidState has no branch for it.
+                #
+                # So put the bid back on that path. PREREFUND is not a chosen
+                # state; it is what process_XMR_SWAP_A_LOCK_tx_spend sets on
+                # seeing the very fact this branch tested for. Nothing is
+                # built and nothing is published -- the engine's own CSV
+                # maturity checks decide what happens next.
+                bid.setState(BidStates.XMR_SWAP_SCRIPT_TX_PREREFUND)
+                self.activateBid(cursor, bid)
+                self.saveBidInSession(bid_id, bid, cursor, xmr_swap)
+                self.commitDB()
+                self.log.info(
+                    f"PWNDA-PATCH-30: returned stalled bid {self.log.id(bid_id)} "
+                    f"to the timelock path (was {state_before})."
+                )
                 return {
-                    "recovered": False,
-                    "state": state_before,
-                    "reason": "A refund is already in flight for this swap; the timelock path will complete it.",
+                    "recovered": True,
+                    "state_before": state_before,
+                    "state": strBidState(bid.state),
+                    "reason": "A refund is in flight. The swap has been put back on the timelock path so the node drives it again.",
                 }
             # PWNDA-PATCH-27 -- Gate 2b: the engine's own record says the
             # chain-A redeem was PUBLISHED. When the chain agrees (>= 1
